May not like the results
but we're comfortable.

00:11:11.574 --> 00:11:13.601
No, on a conscious level

00:11:13.601 --> 00:11:15.020
everything is going crazy.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.947
On a conscious level, we experience doubt.

00:11:17.947 --> 00:11:20.463
The doubt turns into
an emotion called fear

00:11:20.463 --> 00:11:24.742
and that fear is expressed
through the body as anxiety.

00:11:24.742 --> 00:11:27.377
See that person is getting
emotionally involved

00:11:27.377 --> 00:11:28.402
to move ahead.

00:11:28.402 --> 00:11:29.507
Do you know what happens?

00:11:29.507 --> 00:11:32.166
They hit that terror barrier
and they bounce off it

00:11:32.166 --> 00:11:34.913
and right back into bondage.

00:11:34.913 --> 00:11:38.413
And they're so relieved to get back there.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.939
They're back where they're comfortable.

00:11:41.939 --> 00:11:44.172
They've canceled the sale.

00:11:44.172 --> 00:11:46.836
They've decided not to move.

00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:49.556
They're going to stay in the
job that they don't like.

00:11:49.556 --> 00:11:51.820
At least they're comfortable.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.949
Now that's not a very good way to live.

00:11:54.949 --> 00:11:55.902
And you know something?

00:11:55.902 --> 00:11:58.402
That's something everybody experiences

00:11:58.402 --> 00:11:59.701
if they're going to grow.

00:11:59.701 --> 00:12:02.352
You're going to hit that terror barrier.

00:12:02.352 --> 00:12:05.689
See the terror barrier is
going beyond where you're at.

00:12:05.689 --> 00:12:07.479
Going to a new level.

00:12:07.479 --> 00:12:08.949
I'm going to tell you something.

00:12:08.949 --> 00:12:10.967
When I set a goal

00:12:10.967 --> 00:12:15.051
if it doesn't scare and
excite me at the same time

00:12:15.051 --> 00:12:17.503
I know I'm going in the wrong direction.

00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:19.602
Now I also understand

00:12:19.602 --> 00:12:21.885
that my paradigm is
going to try and get me

00:12:21.885 --> 00:12:23.849
to bounce back to where I was.

00:12:23.849 --> 00:12:26.599
It doesn't want me to move ahead.

00:12:28.192 --> 00:12:29.859
I don't want to live there.

00:12:29.859 --> 00:12:32.613
I lived there for the
first 26 years of my life.

00:12:32.613 --> 00:12:35.834
And for the last 50, I've
had a phenomenal life

00:12:35.834 --> 00:12:37.489
and it just keeps getting better.

00:12:37.489 --> 00:12:39.179
And I want you to do the same thing.

00:12:39.179 --> 00:12:40.717
Understand what I've just said.

00:12:40.717 --> 00:12:42.275
I'm going to back this up.

00:12:42.275 --> 00:12:45.233
They got emotionally
involved in the Y idea

00:12:45.233 --> 00:12:47.487
that moved their body into
a different vibration.

00:12:47.487 --> 00:12:49.496
On a conscious level, they're experiencing

00:12:49.496 --> 00:12:50.821
some crazy stuff.

00:12:50.821 --> 00:12:52.220
They start to doubt their ability.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.571
"Oh I'll never be able to pay for it."

00:12:53.571 --> 00:12:55.266
They experience fear.

00:12:55.266 --> 00:12:58.349
The fear expresses itself as anxiety.

00:12:59.833 --> 00:13:02.331
And bang, you bounce
off that terror barrier

00:13:02.331 --> 00:13:04.747
and you're right back.

00:13:04.747 --> 00:13:08.270
"I might not be earning much
here but I know what it is."

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.718
"I would love to move there
but I'm comfortable here.

00:13:10.718 --> 00:13:12.163
"I think I'll just stay here."

00:13:12.163 --> 00:13:14.010
These people are acting
like they have a contract

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.512
to live forever and they don't.

00:13:16.512 --> 00:13:17.345
Do you know what to do?

00:13:17.345 --> 00:13:18.496
Say I'm going to get rid of all that.

00:13:18.496 --> 00:13:21.176
I understand it's there, but
I don't want any part of it.

00:13:21.176 --> 00:13:25.689
And I'm going to go crashing
right through that terror barrier.

00:13:25.689 --> 00:13:27.316
Now does that get rid of the X energy?

00:13:27.316 --> 00:13:30.649
No, the X energy is still there you see.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.532
But at least you're over into freedom.

00:13:33.532 --> 00:13:35.469
You made the move, you did it.

00:13:35.469 --> 00:13:39.037
And if you continue to
feed the right information

00:13:39.037 --> 00:13:42.385
into your mind, keep feeding that Y idea

00:13:42.385 --> 00:13:44.588
keep getting emotionally
involved in the Y idea.

00:13:44.588 --> 00:13:46.887
You're there, you're on the road.

00:13:46.887 --> 00:13:47.962
Keep doing that.

00:13:47.962 --> 00:13:51.602
You're going to find that the
paradigm is going to change

00:13:51.602 --> 00:13:54.786
and it will just all go away.

00:13:54.786 --> 00:13:56.587
And you know where you're living?

00:13:56.587 --> 00:14:01.358
In freedom, you're living
where you want to live.

00:14:01.358 --> 00:14:04.941
Buyers remorse is when
you cancel the sale.

00:14:06.215 --> 00:14:08.329
Buyers remorse is when
you stop just before

00:14:08.329 --> 00:14:10.432
you buy what you really want.

00:14:10.432 --> 00:14:11.664
Before you go for the thing

00:14:11.664 --> 00:14:15.646
that's going to change
your life and you know it.

00:14:15.646 --> 00:14:17.498
It's not moving to the other city.

00:14:17.498 --> 00:14:19.784
It's not starting the
business of your dreams.

00:14:19.784 --> 00:14:23.227
It's not stepping out
and betting on yourself.

00:14:23.227 --> 00:14:25.996
That's a terror barrier
that's causing that.

00:14:25.996 --> 00:14:28.549
And if you don't learn to go
through the terror barrier

00:14:28.549 --> 00:14:29.382
I'm going to tell you something

00:14:29.382 --> 00:14:31.375
you're going to stay right where you are

00:14:31.375 --> 00:14:33.161
for the rest of your days.

00:14:33.161 --> 00:14:35.191
That's not a good place to be.

00:14:35.191 --> 00:14:37.954
What did Joseph Campbell say?

00:14:37.954 --> 00:14:38.787
So true.

00:14:40.285 --> 00:14:45.103
"The cave you fear to enter
holds the treasure you seek."

00:14:45.103 --> 00:14:46.132
- Starting with Lincoln Lawyer

00:14:46.132 --> 00:14:48.112
was a time when I said
I wanted to recalibrate

00:14:48.112 --> 00:14:49.969
my relationship with my career.

00:14:49.969 --> 00:14:52.019
I remember saying that, I
remember thinking my career is

00:14:52.019 --> 00:14:53.875
I'm enjoying it.

00:14:53.875 --> 00:14:56.346
I love what it's given
me, I like going to work.

00:14:56.346 --> 00:14:58.241
I like the things I've been doing

00:14:58.241 --> 00:14:59.311
but everything I started reading.

00:14:59.311 --> 00:15:03.404
I felt like oh, it's another
version of something I've done

00:15:03.404 --> 00:15:04.914
or I feel like I can do it next week.

00:15:04.914 --> 00:15:06.262
And I remember going, well wait a minute.

00:15:06.262 --> 00:15:07.600
Before you get mad at thinking you can

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:08.842
do something next week

00:15:08.842 --> 00:15:10.477
that's a valid feeling.

00:15:10.477 --> 00:15:11.865
Don't just say no to something
because you feel like

00:15:11.865 --> 00:15:13.324
you can actually do it.

00:15:13.324 --> 00:15:15.184
But then I said okay, fair.

00:15:15.184 --> 00:15:16.937
I'll shake with you on
that McConaughey but.

00:15:16.937 --> 00:15:19.542
(audience laughs)

00:15:19.542 --> 00:15:22.574
Let me find something
that I don't know how

00:15:22.574 --> 00:15:24.730
or what to do with that
next week or the week after.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.502
Let me find something that I really like

00:15:26.502 --> 00:15:29.587
but I'm going oh, I'm not sure.

00:15:29.587 --> 00:15:32.133
Them that scares me that shakes my floor.

00:15:32.133 --> 00:15:34.300
And I was fortunate enough

00:15:37.173 --> 00:15:39.753
because that schedule F check I got

00:15:39.753 --> 00:15:40.679
in Angels in the Outfield

00:15:40.679 --> 00:15:42.194
to know that my rent was paid.

00:15:42.194 --> 00:15:43.747
I was fortunate enough to know
my kids were going to eat.

00:15:43.747 --> 00:15:45.943
I was just shepherding my
first son into the world.

00:15:45.943 --> 00:15:48.584
So I had that to take care of my time.

00:15:48.584 --> 00:15:50.349
And I said it's a great
time to go into the shadows

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:53.263
and be a father and sit back

00:15:53.263 --> 00:15:55.658
and see if something turns
you on from the inside out.

00:15:55.658 --> 00:15:57.586
If something finds you,
if you're the target

00:15:57.586 --> 00:15:58.442
that can draw in the air.

00:15:58.442 --> 00:15:59.623
But let's, we're okay.

00:15:59.623 --> 00:16:01.223
Rent's paid, kids are going to eat.

00:16:01.223 --> 00:16:02.950
We can take some time off.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.305
I no way was thinking, "Oh I'm done."

00:16:05.305 --> 00:16:07.080
But I didn't know how long
the dry spell was going to go.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.847
So I said no to some of the things

00:16:08.847 --> 00:16:11.033
that were similar to what
I had been doing before

00:16:11.033 --> 00:16:12.054
and it took a while.

00:16:12.054 --> 00:16:13.440
I had to sit down with my agent and say

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:15.119
"Hey, I'm really going to do this.

00:16:15.119 --> 00:16:16.898
"I need your help with
my commitment to this

00:16:16.898 --> 00:16:20.921
"Because after eight months
if the same thing comes in

00:16:20.921 --> 00:16:22.649
"With the big 10 million dollar paycheck

00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:24.126
"It starts to read better."

00:16:24.126 --> 00:16:26.959
(audience laughs)

00:16:27.951 --> 00:16:29.329
It just does, I promise you.

00:16:29.329 --> 00:16:31.162
I mean the same words.

00:16:32.004 --> 00:16:34.574
(audience laughs)

00:16:34.574 --> 00:16:37.511
Suddenly it's kind of, I
think this thing's great.

00:16:37.511 --> 00:16:40.036
(audience laughs)

00:16:40.036 --> 00:16:41.492
I think I can find an angle.

00:16:41.492 --> 00:16:44.644
No, I can make it a different experience.

00:16:44.644 --> 00:16:45.661
So I said, "I'm going to need your help

00:16:45.661 --> 00:16:48.823
"Hunkering down here and
saying no to some things

00:16:48.823 --> 00:16:50.719
"And so I'm going to need
you to be a gate keeper.

00:16:50.719 --> 00:16:52.890
"One to keep from being
too, let's be real clear.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:57.104
"I'm looking for some
different things to do."

00:16:57.104 --> 00:16:59.303
He held up, he handled that.

00:16:59.303 --> 00:17:01.320
My wife, we said we don't know
how long it's going to be dry.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.346
Then after they quit sending me those

00:17:04.346 --> 00:17:05.179
then it did get dry.

00:17:05.179 --> 00:17:06.998
Then nothing came for about a year.

00:17:06.998 --> 00:17:08.462
There was nothing.

00:17:08.462 --> 00:17:11.625
And I didn't have any sleepless nights

00:17:11.625 --> 00:17:14.134
or oh my gosh, it was like
no I'll find something.

00:17:14.134 --> 00:17:16.474
I'll write, I was writing a lot.

00:17:16.474 --> 00:17:18.086
I was turning myself on creatively

00:17:18.086 --> 00:17:19.734
and as I've said, I had
my first son to shepherd

00:17:19.734 --> 00:17:20.585
into the world.

00:17:20.585 --> 00:17:22.405
And then the funny thing happened.

00:17:22.405 --> 00:17:23.414
The beautiful thing happened.

00:17:23.414 --> 00:17:26.999
That somehow the target drew the arrow

00:17:26.999 --> 00:17:28.939
and I think my opinion is

00:17:28.939 --> 00:17:31.022
I became a new good idea.

00:17:32.494 --> 00:17:34.077
By removing myself.

00:17:35.451 --> 00:17:37.739
I became William Friedkin
calls for the first.

00:17:37.739 --> 00:17:39.327
Steven Soderbergh calls
for the first time.

00:17:39.327 --> 00:17:42.179
Somehow in that two years,
I became a fresh new idea

00:17:42.179 --> 00:17:46.297
that I don't think I was
two, three years prior.

00:17:46.297 --> 00:17:47.749
How that works, I'm not sure

00:17:47.749 --> 00:17:49.251
because I didn't send a memo out.

00:17:49.251 --> 00:17:51.438
(audience laughs)

00:17:51.438 --> 00:17:52.288
You know?

00:17:52.288 --> 00:17:53.558
But it did happen.

00:17:53.558 --> 00:17:55.051
- The people who've
been living a caged life

00:17:55.051 --> 00:17:56.113
after a period of time

00:17:56.113 --> 00:17:57.525
of watching enough people go by

00:17:57.525 --> 00:17:58.958
who are succeeding

00:17:58.958 --> 00:18:01.172
if maturity lands on them

00:18:01.172 --> 00:18:02.727
it lands on them with an impulse to say

00:18:02.727 --> 00:18:07.038
"I've got to take control
over the direction of my life.

00:18:07.038 --> 00:18:08.807
"I've got to break free from these bars

00:18:08.807 --> 00:18:10.498
"Because I've set them up."

00:18:10.498 --> 00:18:12.930
At some point, we come to
realize I think in maturity

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:14.422
that we set our own cages.

00:18:14.422 --> 00:18:16.578
We build our own bars.

00:18:16.578 --> 00:18:18.833
And that there was always a door over here

00:18:18.833 --> 00:18:19.949
that we could get out of

00:18:19.949 --> 00:18:22.776
but we never made the choice to.

00:18:22.776 --> 00:18:25.601
And when we finally
decide to change our life

00:18:25.601 --> 00:18:27.267
we're more likely to go out that door

00:18:27.267 --> 00:18:28.437
but we always have to remember

00:18:28.437 --> 00:18:30.569
you know, never forget that when you knock

00:18:30.569 --> 00:18:32.107
on the door of opportunity

00:18:32.107 --> 00:18:34.907
that it is work who answers.

00:18:34.907 --> 00:18:37.408
You know, it's going to take a
lot of work to change your life.

00:18:37.408 --> 00:18:39.697
To break free from the
bars, to get going again.

00:18:39.697 --> 00:18:40.971
But I think that's the great opportunity.

00:18:40.971 --> 00:18:43.233
And when people finally
break through that cage

00:18:43.233 --> 00:18:44.259
and they get out in the open

00:18:44.259 --> 00:18:45.678
and have more freedom in their life

00:18:45.678 --> 00:18:47.586
that kind of life has a quality too.

00:18:47.586 --> 00:18:49.895
It feels incredibly different.

00:18:49.895 --> 00:18:52.723
That kind of life feels more free.

00:18:52.723 --> 00:18:54.833
And that kind of life over a
period of time is incredible

00:18:54.833 --> 00:18:56.868
because you have more
freedom to direct yourself

00:18:56.868 --> 00:18:57.868
more freedom to do things

00:18:57.868 --> 00:19:01.233
and what ends up is people
end up with deeper skills.

00:19:01.233 --> 00:19:04.070
They end up you know, chasing
their passions more often.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:05.741
That often as they get on a roll

00:19:05.741 --> 00:19:07.464
they start becoming more successful.

00:19:07.464 --> 00:19:08.793
As they become more successful

00:19:08.793 --> 00:19:10.988
the things they think that
they wanted in their lives

00:19:10.988 --> 00:19:12.024
come into their lives.

00:19:12.024 --> 00:19:14.262
You know, they got the two car garage

00:19:14.262 --> 00:19:16.315
the white picket fence, the house

00:19:16.315 --> 00:19:19.243
the kids, the friends, the dinner parties.

00:19:19.243 --> 00:19:22.532
You know, enough to get by
and maybe a little bit more.

00:19:22.532 --> 00:19:23.978
And soon after a period of time

00:19:23.978 --> 00:19:26.596
that excitement of that breaking free

00:19:26.596 --> 00:19:28.357
and getting into that new kind of life

00:19:28.357 --> 00:19:31.144
that kind of life, it
feels more comfortable.

00:19:31.144 --> 00:19:33.269
So we call it the comfortable life.

00:19:33.269 --> 00:19:35.851
And in that comfortable
life, we do feel that way.

00:19:35.851 --> 00:19:37.605
We feel a sense of satisfaction.

00:19:37.605 --> 00:19:40.457
A greater sense of
confidence about who we are.

00:19:40.457 --> 00:19:42.101
About what life is really about.

00:19:42.101 --> 00:19:43.440
About where we're going in life.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:45.875
We feel heightened degrees of competency.

00:19:45.875 --> 00:19:47.608
Knowledge, skills, abilities.

00:19:47.608 --> 00:19:49.765
We feel like we kind of
got our life under control.

00:19:49.765 --> 00:19:51.098
Things are good.

00:19:52.442 --> 00:19:54.066
But over a period of time
in the comfortable life

00:19:54.066 --> 00:19:56.840
something also rattles
within and stirs within.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.138
Maybe not a frustration

00:19:58.138 --> 00:20:01.223
but maybe somewhat of a
sense of restlessness.

00:20:01.223 --> 00:20:03.320
And that restlessness is this feeling

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.983
and this sense that maybe
there is something more.

00:20:05.983 --> 00:20:07.446
And people who have a comfortable life

00:20:07.446 --> 00:20:09.675
they also have a communication pattern.

00:20:09.675 --> 00:20:11.817
They also say something
on a recurring basis

00:20:11.817 --> 00:20:14.028
that you can tell they're
in a comfortable life.

00:20:14.028 --> 00:20:15.696
Because what ends up happening is one day

00:20:15.696 --> 00:20:18.528
someone says to you, "So
how's everything going?"

00:20:18.528 --> 00:20:22.588
And even though you have
all the reason in the world

00:20:22.588 --> 00:20:24.755
to say, "Life is amazing."

00:20:25.816 --> 00:20:27.920
You find yourself and hear
yourself starting saying

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:29.322
when people ask how your life is going

00:20:29.322 --> 00:20:31.572
you say, "Well, it's fine."

00:20:34.534 --> 00:20:38.701
And the "It's fine" is the
tell of the comfortable life.

00:20:39.859 --> 00:20:42.154
It's the tell that there
must be something more.

00:20:42.154 --> 00:20:45.147
There most be another
quality, another kind of life

00:20:45.147 --> 00:20:47.886
and that reveals to us that
there is this other thing

00:20:47.886 --> 00:20:50.688
called the charged life.

00:20:50.688 --> 00:20:53.442
And the charged life
has a different quality

00:20:53.442 --> 00:20:54.358
and feel to it as well.

00:20:54.358 --> 00:20:55.891
That there's heightened levels

00:20:55.891 --> 00:20:58.368
of first and foremost, energy there.

00:20:58.368 --> 00:21:00.223
People are more passionate
when they're living

00:21:00.223 --> 00:21:01.133
the charged life

00:21:01.133 --> 00:21:02.390
and because they are more passionate

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:03.871
they feel more of the charge.

00:21:03.871 --> 00:21:05.451
It's not a one time spark.

00:21:05.451 --> 00:21:07.111
It's not once in a while I feel good.

00:21:07.111 --> 00:21:10.275
It's an enduring state of passion

00:21:10.275 --> 00:21:12.539
and happiness and satisfaction.

00:21:12.539 --> 00:21:15.342
But it's an enduring
state that is triggered

00:21:15.342 --> 00:21:16.827
not by comfort

00:21:16.827 --> 00:21:19.433
but rather by challenge.

00:21:19.433 --> 00:21:21.996
That when we challenge ourselves
to go just a little beyond

00:21:21.996 --> 00:21:23.777
our current competencies

00:21:23.777 --> 00:21:25.315
our knowledge, skills, and abilities

00:21:25.315 --> 00:21:26.357
when we're willing to push ourselves

00:21:26.357 --> 00:21:27.782
just a little bit further

00:21:27.782 --> 00:21:29.712
that's when we start to feel a charge.

00:21:29.712 --> 00:21:32.104
Because so much of what
we know by neuroscience

00:21:32.104 --> 00:21:33.988
and what actually charges our brains

00:21:33.988 --> 00:21:37.149
of what actually enlivens us in our brains

00:21:37.149 --> 00:21:39.650
and what we can see by
oxygenation, blood flow

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.437
to specific parts of our brain

00:21:41.437 --> 00:21:44.369
to the hormonal releases, we
can measure back of our brain

00:21:44.369 --> 00:21:46.567
from whether it's dopamine, vasopressin

00:21:46.567 --> 00:21:49.725
oxytocin, serotonin,
these things often happen

00:21:49.725 --> 00:21:52.593
because we're heightening engaged

00:21:52.593 --> 00:21:53.574
with something that's challenging us

00:21:53.574 --> 00:21:56.279
just a little beyond our current level.

00:21:56.279 --> 00:21:59.400
Like Mihály Csíkszentmihályi
talks about it in psychology

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:01.520
as this concept of flow.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:04.480
Of doing something where
we're so engaged with it

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.689
and you're so engaged with it

00:22:05.689 --> 00:22:08.862
because it's just a little
bit harder than usual.

00:22:08.862 --> 00:22:10.255
So you're not quite comfortable

00:22:10.255 --> 00:22:11.786
you're just a little
bit out of comfort zone.

00:22:11.786 --> 00:22:14.394
Not totally out of comfort
zone and completely overwhelmed

00:22:14.394 --> 00:22:18.309
but appropriately challenged
to stretch yourself.

00:22:18.309 --> 00:22:21.426
And the qualities that the
charged life basically has

00:22:21.426 --> 00:22:23.901
are there's a heightened and
sustained level of energy

00:22:23.901 --> 00:22:26.818
and engagement but also enthusiasm.

00:22:27.745 --> 00:22:29.429
And that's the magic.

00:22:29.429 --> 00:22:31.446
You know, if you want to
have a fully charged life

00:22:31.446 --> 00:22:33.993
you have to start looking
forward to things again.

00:22:33.993 --> 00:22:36.054
You have to get excited
about tomorrow again.

00:22:36.054 --> 00:22:37.873
You have to see your
life developing again.

00:22:37.873 --> 00:22:40.488
You have to set yourself on a path

00:22:40.488 --> 00:22:43.213
where you're step-by-step
progressing every single day

00:22:43.213 --> 00:22:45.098
so you know tomorrow's going to be better

00:22:45.098 --> 00:22:46.121
that it was today.

00:22:46.121 --> 00:22:48.134
That you know tomorrow,
you're going to become more

00:22:48.134 --> 00:22:50.059
of who you know you can become.

00:22:50.059 --> 00:22:52.399
That you know tomorrow,
by your simple choices

00:22:52.399 --> 00:22:55.435
by your simple sets of
disciplines and habits

00:22:55.435 --> 00:22:56.923
that you're going to evolve

00:22:56.923 --> 00:22:58.840
into your highest self.

00:22:59.906 --> 00:23:02.574
And that is the path of the charged life.

00:23:02.574 --> 00:23:05.628
This constant engagement
with the best within us

00:23:05.628 --> 00:23:06.951
of pushing ourselves

00:23:06.951 --> 00:23:08.817
but with that purpose and that progress

00:23:08.817 --> 00:23:11.400
of hoping to become our highest selves.

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:12.945
And when you live in that place

00:23:12.945 --> 00:23:14.837
and you sense that every single day

00:23:14.837 --> 00:23:18.643
that's the magic, that's
what life should feel like.

00:23:18.643 --> 00:23:20.245
That's what I think we all deserve

00:23:20.245 --> 00:23:22.102
and maybe we ought to start aiming

00:23:22.102 --> 00:23:23.515
and challenging ourselves
just a little bit more

00:23:23.515 --> 00:23:24.598
to get there.

00:23:25.452 --> 00:23:27.379
- My take is the best way
to leave your comfort zone

00:23:27.379 --> 00:23:30.342
is to recognize that
you're playing inside it.

00:23:30.342 --> 00:23:32.113
I think this is the biggest challenge

00:23:32.113 --> 00:23:33.318
of leaving your comfort zone.

00:23:33.318 --> 00:23:36.175
Is we're so used to playing
inside our comfort zone

00:23:36.175 --> 00:23:37.921
that we don't want to step outside it.

00:23:37.921 --> 00:23:39.131
We don't even have the awareness

00:23:39.131 --> 00:23:40.547
that we're playing small.

00:23:40.547 --> 00:23:42.363
I had this T-shirt that I like to wear

00:23:42.363 --> 00:23:43.410
I haven't worn it a while on the channel

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:45.416
but maybe we can find an old video

00:23:45.416 --> 00:23:48.884
where there's this thing
of one circle that says

00:23:48.884 --> 00:23:49.861
"Your comfort zone."

00:23:49.861 --> 00:23:51.844
And there's another circle
outside of it that says

00:23:51.844 --> 00:23:53.054
"Where the magic happens."

00:23:53.054 --> 00:23:54.316
So you want to stop playing here

00:23:54.316 --> 00:23:56.337
and you want to play out
here where the magic happens.

00:23:56.337 --> 00:23:58.574
And I think having the
awareness to understand

00:23:58.574 --> 00:24:00.890
that you are playing small right now

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:04.794
is super, super, super,
super, super duper important.

00:24:04.794 --> 00:24:06.544
Because what happens is
we like to play safe.

00:24:06.544 --> 00:24:08.813
We like to be comfortable,
we like to stay in the world

00:24:08.813 --> 00:24:10.334
that we know of, it's comfortable.

00:24:10.334 --> 00:24:12.336
It's warm, we've done it before.

00:24:12.336 --> 00:24:13.809
It's easy to stay there.

00:24:13.809 --> 00:24:15.577
You don't want to go out into the unknown

00:24:15.577 --> 00:24:17.311
into the scary, into the cold

00:24:17.311 --> 00:24:18.850
into the who knows what's going to happen

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:20.235
into the risky zone.

00:24:20.235 --> 00:24:23.485
And so, that's a lot of fear out there.

00:24:24.454 --> 00:24:26.359
That's a lot of fear living way out here.

00:24:26.359 --> 00:24:29.110
And what really happens is
we find practical reasons

00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:30.561
to stay inside our box.

00:24:30.561 --> 00:24:31.849
We find practical reasons.

00:24:31.849 --> 00:24:34.480
Like, oh well we don't have
the money to go out there.

00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:36.143
Or I didn't have the
education to go out there.

00:24:36.143 --> 00:24:37.632
Or like, you know I don't have the time

00:24:37.632 --> 00:24:38.766
to go out and do that thing.

00:24:38.766 --> 00:24:40.391
I'm not really interested in doing that.

00:24:40.391 --> 00:24:42.582
We find these reasons
and we convince ourselves

00:24:42.582 --> 00:24:43.745
that these reasons are true.

00:24:43.745 --> 00:24:46.213
And really all they are, are mechanisms

00:24:46.213 --> 00:24:48.475
to keep you inside your safe box

00:24:48.475 --> 00:24:50.011
inside your comfort zone.

00:24:50.011 --> 00:24:53.556
Where that happens so subconsciously

00:24:53.556 --> 00:24:55.349
and the trick comes to understanding

00:24:55.349 --> 00:24:57.802
that all of those reasons
aren't really true.

00:24:57.802 --> 00:24:58.735
It's just fear.

00:24:58.735 --> 00:24:59.952
It's not that you're not interested in it.

00:24:59.952 --> 00:25:01.463
It's not that you don't
have the time to do it.

00:25:01.463 --> 00:25:02.423
You're just afraid.

00:25:02.423 --> 00:25:03.559
You're afraid it's not going to work.

00:25:03.559 --> 00:25:04.744
You're afraid you're going to lose money.

00:25:04.744 --> 00:25:06.001
You're afraid of embarrassing yourself.

00:25:06.001 --> 00:25:07.438
You're afraid of the un, you're afraid.

00:25:07.438 --> 00:25:09.622
And once you recognize that it's fear

00:25:09.622 --> 00:25:10.514
that's holding you back

00:25:10.514 --> 00:25:12.365
instead of a logical, practical reason.

00:25:12.365 --> 00:25:14.287
Having that awareness

00:25:14.287 --> 00:25:15.837
when you've figured that out

00:25:15.837 --> 00:25:17.655
then you can more easily make the switch

00:25:17.655 --> 00:25:19.327
thinking outside your comfort zone.

00:25:19.327 --> 00:25:20.876
But as long as you've convinced yourself

00:25:20.876 --> 00:25:23.742
that it's a smart decision
to stay where you are

00:25:23.742 --> 00:25:24.643
then guess what?

00:25:24.643 --> 00:25:26.233
You're going to stay where you are

00:25:26.233 --> 00:25:27.850
and you're never going to
leave your comfort zone.

00:25:27.850 --> 00:25:30.777
So having the awareness is
the most important part.

00:25:30.777 --> 00:25:32.126
And once you have the awareness

00:25:32.126 --> 00:25:34.380
then it's having the courage
to push through the fear

00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:35.897
to achieve your goals

00:25:35.897 --> 00:25:37.610
and step outside your comfort zone.

00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:39.224
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:25:39.224 --> 00:25:42.347
I made this video because
Syed Wajahat asked me to.

00:25:42.347 --> 00:25:43.825
So if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:25:43.825 --> 00:25:45.680
